// gpu16 global memory test data, used by gpu_global, gpu_gstore,
// gpu_gwide and gpu_coalesce.
//
// The rule is one line long: the byte at address a holds a & 0xff.
// A 32 bit word at address 4n is therefore
//     ((4n+3)&0xff)<<24 | ((4n+2)&0xff)<<16 | ((4n+1)&0xff)<<8 | (4n&0xff)
// which makes every expectation in those four tests a function of the
// address alone, so a load that lands one byte or one lane out of place
// cannot accidentally match.
// 1024 words = 4096 bytes = 64 aligned 64-byte transactions.
